73
00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.460
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:26.317 --> 00:04:29.152
Grammar focus: Future perfect continuous.

75
00:04:29.452 --> 00:04:30.674
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:31.383 --> 00:04:34.648
By next year, I will have been working toward this goal.

77
00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:38.316
By June, she will have been training for two years.

78
00:04:39.217 --> 00:04:43.457
By 2030, we will have been studying English for ten years.

79
00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:49.708
Use this tense to look back from a point in the future and say how long an action will have continued.

80
00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:55.041
Be careful! Don't say: By next year, I will have been work toward this goal.

81
00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.706
Say: By next year, I will have been working toward this goal.

82
00:05:01.006 --> 00:05:03.447
After 'will have been', use the -ing form.

83
